---
import PageLayout from "../../../components/PageLayout.astro";
import { releases } from "../../../data/releases";
---
<PageLayout lang="en" active="roadmap" title="Release Log — Linxira OS" maxWidth="860px">
  <h1>Release Log</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Released ISO builds. The current image is {releases.iso.label}, with the next build expected in November; Arch is a rolling release, so old images are never retained — only their SHA256 is recorded.</p>
  <div class="section-divider"></div>

  <div class="rel-item reveal">
    <div class="rel-head">
      <code class="rel-name">{releases.iso.filename}</code>
      <span class="tag latest">Latest</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rel-meta">{releases.iso.date} · {releases.iso.sizeHuman} · SHA256 <code class="sha">{releases.iso.sha256}</code></div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>KDE Plasma is the only recommended desktop</b>: terminal, system settings, updates, and configuration entries are verified there; defects on other desktops (including COSMIC) are fixed gradually across build cycles — do not use them for daily work in the meantime</li>
      <li>Welcome 1.2.1 adds a System page driven by <code>capabilities.json</code></li>
      <li>config-hub 2.6.1: <code>linxira-config capabilities --json</code> plus the linxira-config skill</li>
      <li>crash-watch 0.1.2 copyable prompts; hooks 1.1.3 fixes the os-release symlink</li>
      <li>Installer boot/ESP gating and multi-size GRUB theme; Zeta 1.4.4-1 and catalog 3.6.0 onboard</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="rel-note">
      <p><b>Known issues in this build</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Zeta 1.4.4 is unstable on Linux; prefer npm, solidly fixed from 1.4.6 onward</li>
        <li><b>COSMIC: config, update, and crash-triage entries do not open or close immediately</b>: the image dispatches <code>cosmic-term -e</code>, but <code>cosmic-term</code> has no <code>-e</code> (only <code>--working-directory</code>), so the argument is read as a file and the process exits at once. Fixed and shipped as packages: <code>linxira-config-hub 2.6.2</code>, <code>linxira-update 0.1.10</code>, <code>linxira-crash-watch 0.1.3</code>; run <code>sudo pacman -Syu</code> and reopen the entry. Plasma is unaffected</li>
        <li><b>The first <code>linxira-update</code> may report "No synced pacman repository"</b>: when the install-time <code>[linxira]</code> database pre-sync fails, installed packages are misread as foreign. From <code>linxira-update 0.1.10</code> the tool retries <code>pacman -Sy</code> and re-detects automatically; older versions need one manual <code>sudo pacman -Sy</code></li>
        <li>Headphones or speakers may click briefly at power-on; hardware-level noise, not addressed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Cadence and update frequency</h2>
  <p>Only images actually uploaded to the cloud count as released; internal builds are not part of the release record. <b>Images are built roughly every 25–45 days</b>, depending on schedule and capacity — not a hard commitment. Because Arch is a rolling release, an ISO only reflects its build day, so <b>old images are not retained or offered; only each version's SHA256 is recorded</b>. Packages roll with Arch, so the signed <code>[linxira]</code> repository can be updated at any time — day-to-day fixes ship as package updates and need no image rebuild; the WSL image follows each batch.</p>
  <table class="hist-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Series</th><th>Build date</th><th>Since previous in series</th><th>Type</th><th>Cloud</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>{releases.iso.date}</td><td>1 day</td><td>Fix round r4 (current)</td><td class="cur">Released</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>2026-10-26</td><td>26 days</td><td>Monthly image</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>WSL</td><td>{releases.wsl.date}</td><td>26 days</td><td>WSL image (current)</td><td class="cur">Released</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>2026-09-30</td><td>1 day</td><td>Fix round r17</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>WSL</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>—</td><td>WSL v1.1</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>8 days</td><td>Fix rounds r12–r14</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>2026-09-21</td><td>38 days</td><td>Fix rounds r2–r4</td><td>Not released</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ISO</td><td>2026-08-09 → 08-14</td><td>—</td><td>Daily iteration / test baseline</td><td>Not released</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Upload history (old builds deleted)</h2>
  <p>These builds were uploaded at the dates shown and have all been deleted since. Every download site keeps <b>only the newest release and its assets</b>: the system is a rolling Arch release, old images are no longer maintained, and support requests for them are not accepted.</p>
  <table class="hist-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Size</th><th>SHA256</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>{releases.wsl.filename.replace('-x86_64.tar.gz', '')}</td><td>{releases.wsl.date}</td><td>{releases.wsl.sizeHuman}</td><td><code>{releases.wsl.sha256Short}</code></td><td class="cur">Latest (kept)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.30-r17</td><td>2026-09-30</td><td>5.14 GB</td><td><code>9162b270…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.29-r14</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>5.15 GB</td><td><code>f9413317…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.29-r13</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>—</td><td><code>31fd005c…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.29-r12</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>—</td><td><code>174acbe2…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-wsl-2026.09.29</td><td>2026-09-29</td><td>488 MB</td><td><code>b5b7b485…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.28</td><td>2026-09-28</td><td>—</td><td><code>63a20c95…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.27</td><td>2026-09-27</td><td>—</td><td><code>1f832cc3…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.08.14</td><td>2026-08-14</td><td>4.79 GB</td><td><code>b85ffcea…</code></td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--faint);">The 2026-10-26 series went through five incremental builds (installer 134 fix, build-time expected versions, unified boot branding); only the final build of a series is published, intermediate builds are not distributed.</p>
<p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--faint);">2026-08-14 is the earliest test build: features were incomplete — it only validated that installation completes and that some first-party system software starts.</p>

  <h2>Internal builds (never uploaded)</h2>
  <p>These images were only produced on the build machine and were never uploaded, so they are not release records and are not offered for download. Listed for internal traceability only.</p>
  <table class="hist-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Size</th><th>SHA256</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.21r4</td><td>2026-09-21</td><td>5.09 GB</td><td><code>b36aec3b…</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.21r3</td><td>2026-09-21</td><td>5.09 GB</td><td><code>4dfb2e87…</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.09.21r2</td><td>2026-09-21</td><td>5.42 GB</td><td><code>d5e1e308…</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.08.13</td><td>2026-08-13</td><td>4.79 GB</td><td><code>b880391c…</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.08.12</td><td>2026-08-12</td><td>4.73 GB</td><td>Not archived</td></tr>
      <tr><td>linxira-2026.08.09-r17</td><td>2026-08-09</td><td>4.69 GB</td><td>Not archived</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div style="text-align:center; margin-top:2.5rem;">
    <a href="/en/download/" class="cta-ghost">Download latest ISO →</a>
  </div>

  <style>
    .subtitle { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .rel-item { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(30,41,59,0.6), rgba(14,20,23,0.8)); border: 1px solid rgba(51,65,85,0.5); border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.2rem 0; }
    .rel-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    .rel-name { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-strong); background: none; padding: 0; }
    .rel-meta { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.82rem; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .sha { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--soft); background: rgba(30,41,59,0.9); padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; word-break: break-all; }
    .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.12rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 99px; font-weight: 600; }
    .tag.latest { background: rgba(32,184,176,0.2); color: #4DD8D0; }
    .tag.stable { background: rgba(32,184,176,0.28); color: #5EEAD4; border: 1px solid rgba(32,184,176,0.4); }
    .tag.beta { background: rgba(234,179,8,0.15); color: #FACC15; }
    .tag.rc { background: rgba(148,163,184,0.15); color: #94a3b8; }
    .rel-item ul { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0.3rem 0 0; }
    .cta-ghost { display: inline-block; padding: 0.85rem 1.8rem; color: var(--ink-strong); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; transition: all 0.2s; }
    .cta-ghost:hover { border-color: var(--teal); color: var(--teal); }
    .hist-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0 1.6rem; font-size: 0.88rem; }
    .hist-table th { text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem; color: var(--faint); font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }
    .hist-table td { padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem; color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(51,65,85,0.35); vertical-align: top; }
    .hist-table code { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--soft); }
    .hist-table .cur { color: #4DD8D0; font-weight: 600; }
  </style>
</PageLayout>
